            <ArticleTitle>Time required for improvement of an analgesic rebound headache.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is typically delayed improvement in analgesic rebound headache after the offending agents have been discontinued. This case history documents that, at times, it might be necessary to omit medications for 6 months until the almost daily headaches cease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
